# Gold final ledger for deterministic syntax and dependency validation.

observation equal-priors
  The prior probabilities of R1, R2, and R3 are each one third.

observation initial-diagnostic-likelihoods
  The original recorded joint likelihoods for (+,-) were 1/4, 1/2, and 3/8.

claim initial-posterior
  CHECKPOINT initial.posterior = [2/9,4/9,1/3]
  Normalizing the equal-prior likelihood weights gives the initial posterior.

link equal-priors supports initial-posterior
link initial-diagnostic-likelihoods supports initial-posterior

claim initial-admissible
  CHECKPOINT initial.admissible = [Q,R]
  Q and R meet the original two-thirds deadline-probability floor.

claim initial-plan
  CHECKPOINT initial.plan = R
  R has the lowest expected loss among the initially admissible plans.

link initial-posterior supports initial-admissible
link initial-admissible supports initial-plan

observation corrected-diagnostic-likelihoods
  The corrected R1 likelihood is 3/4; R2 and R3 remain 1/2 and 3/8.

link corrected-diagnostic-likelihoods revises initial-diagnostic-likelihoods

claim revised-posterior
  CHECKPOINT revised.posterior = [6/13,4/13,3/13]
  Normalizing the corrected likelihood weights gives the revised posterior.

link corrected-diagnostic-likelihoods supports revised-posterior
link revised-posterior revises initial-posterior

claim revised-admissible
  CHECKPOINT revised.admissible = [P,Q,S]
  P, Q, and S meet the corrected deadline-probability floor.

claim revised-plan
  CHECKPOINT revised.plan = P
  P has expected loss 98/13, below S at 100/13 and Q at 102/13.

link revised-posterior supports revised-admissible
link revised-admissible supports revised-plan
link revised-plan revises initial-plan

observation main-positive-signal
  Under P, the positive-signal likelihoods are 1/10, 1, and 1/10.

claim revised-z-posterior
  CHECKPOINT revised.z_posterior = [6/49,40/49,3/49]
  The positive signal updates the corrected main branch.

link revised-posterior supports revised-z-posterior
link main-positive-signal supports revised-z-posterior

claim revised-recovery
  CHECKPOINT revised.recovery = V
  V has expected loss 180/49, below W at 276/49 and U at 347/49.

link revised-z-posterior supports revised-recovery

observation counterfactual-diagnostic
  In the separate (+,+) branch, the joint likelihoods are 5/8, 1/8, and 1/4.

claim counterfactual-posterior
  CHECKPOINT counterfactual.posterior = [5/8,1/8,1/4]
  The counterfactual is normalized from the original equal priors.

link equal-priors supports counterfactual-posterior
link counterfactual-diagnostic supports counterfactual-posterior

claim counterfactual-admissible
  CHECKPOINT counterfactual.admissible = [P,Q,S]
  P, Q, and S meet the counterfactual deadline-probability floor.

claim counterfactual-plan
  CHECKPOINT counterfactual.plan = S
  S has the lowest admissible counterfactual expected loss.

link counterfactual-posterior supports counterfactual-admissible
link counterfactual-admissible supports counterfactual-plan

observation counterfactual-positive-signal
  Under S, the positive-signal likelihoods are 1/20, 1, and 1/10.

claim counterfactual-z-posterior
  CHECKPOINT counterfactual.z_posterior = [5/29,20/29,4/29]
  The positive signal updates only the counterfactual branch.

link counterfactual-posterior supports counterfactual-z-posterior
link counterfactual-positive-signal supports counterfactual-z-posterior

claim counterfactual-recovery
  CHECKPOINT counterfactual.recovery = V
  V has the lowest counterfactual expected recovery loss.

link counterfactual-z-posterior supports counterfactual-recovery

model holds revised-recovery
  confidence 1

model holds counterfactual-recovery
  confidence 1
